#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# clebsch_gordan

#% text
# `clebsch_gordan([j1, m1], [j2, m2], [j, m])` gives the Clebsch-Gordan coefficient for coupling `j1` and `j2` to `j`, exact (a rational times a square root).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Half-integer arguments are allowed; the value is 0 outside the selection rules (`m = m1 + m2`, the triangle condition).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
clebsch_gordan([5, 0], [4, 0], [1, 0])
#% output
#= (1/33)*165^(1/2)

#% cell
clebsch_gordan([1/2, -1/2], [1, 0], [1/2, -1/2])
#% output
#= (-1/3)*3^(1/2)

#% cell
clebsch_gordan([2, 1], [2, 4], [4, 2])
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `three_j_symbol`, `six_j_symbol`, `wigner_d`
